  "_comment": "gnuhr.com rescan 2026-09-04, following the 2026-06-26 pass in gnuhr.json (21 rows in the catalog). Discovery from the maker's own /collections/all (6 pages, ~94 listings); every weight below is quoted from the maker's own product page. Items the maker publishes no weight for were DROPPED, not estimated: Warp Gaiter, Bagdaddy Pants, Power Hoodie (v1), Warp Kit Panel, Gnorda 002, Gnorda 008, Gnorda Retro Socks, Tubular T Ferg Swash, OEM Electrolyte Drink Mix. Warp Kit Rest was dropped too — it publishes two component weights (gloves/sleeves ~160g, neck gaiter ~47g) and no product weight. Colourway and print editions of a garment already listed here were skipped rather than duplicated (Tubular T Orchid/Earthian/Exo-Gnosis/Chrome Smiley/Wish You Were Here/Printed/Retro Polka, the Tubular Tank and Tryptagaiter prints, the PCT editions, Gno Cap Logo, the gift bags). The two Gnorda Dyneema Breaker pieces are already catalogued under the 'Gnuhr x Norda' brand and are not repeated. SLING WEIGHTS: the v3.0 pages carry TWO figures — a numbered spec line and a prose sentence. The spec line is stale: 'weight 23g, dimensions 16cm x 28 cm' is exactly what the Sling 1 v2.0 page still publishes today, and is what the existing 'Sling One' row was built from, so the prose sentence is the v3.0 figure and is what is used here. CW&T is not a catalogued brand, so unlike the Norda collab (both parties catalogued -> 'Gnuhr x Norda') these file under Gnuhr with the product's full title. Breaker Wind Shirt v1.5 was dropped after the audit flagged it: the maker publishes the IDENTICAL figure for it and for the already-catalogued Breaker Wind Shirt ('weight is ~ 71g for size 4' on both pages), so a second row would be indistinguishable by the only thing this catalog stores. Nalgene 16oz carries no variant — the size is in the name.",
